IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`
IMPORT `coa20-part27-merger`
IMPORT `coa-proc-merger`
IMPORT `coa-proc-merger-court-wait`

-- coa-proc-merger-court-wait-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-merger-court-wait.l4 (Companies Act 2006, Part 27, Chapter 2, ss 916, 917 and 918: the one-month wait).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- The dates used throughout: the registrar publishes the notice of receipt on 15 January 2026, so the first date one calendar month later is 15 February 2026,
-- 31 days after the publication; day 30 is 14 February 2026 (one day short) and day 31 is 15 February 2026 (exactly one month). A notice published on 31 January 2026
-- allows an order from 1 March 2026, 29 days later, because 28 February 2026 has 28 January as its date one month before, which is earlier than 31 January.

§ `Tests for the one-month wait of ss 916, 917 and 918`

§§ `Fixtures: dates`

`publication: 15 January 2026` MEANS Date 15 1 2026
`publication: 31 January 2026` MEANS Date 31 1 2026
`publication: 31 January 2028` MEANS Date 31 1 2028
`publication: 1 March 2026` MEANS Date 1 3 2026

§§ `Fixtures: the schemes (the eighteen fields, in order)`

-- the fields, in order: the company is public; a compromise or arrangement is proposed; it is for a reconstruction or amalgamation; the consideration is shares;
-- the company is being wound up; one or more public companies' undertaking is to be transferred; to another existing public company; two or more public companies'
-- undertaking is to be transferred; to a new company; all the relevant securities are held by the transferee; the percentages held; s 915A(3); s 915A(4);
-- s 918A(1); s 916(2); s 917(2); the arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A (a Boolean, from which s 917A(1) is called); s 918(1).
`scheme: absorption, nothing held` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 60), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
-- the same two schemes, but with the transferee company relying on the exemption: the answer of s 916(2) is JUST TRUE for the first, the answer of s 918(1) is JUST TRUE for the second.
`scheme: absorption, all securities held, the transferee relies on section 916(2)` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, (LIST 100), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, nothing held, the transferee relies on section 918(1)` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (LIST 60), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST TRUE)
`scheme: formation of a new company` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, (LIST 0), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)
`scheme: absorption, all securities held` MEANS `ss 902-918 the scheme` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, (LIST 100), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (JUST FALSE)

§§ `Fixtures: the answers read at the date of the order (the second, third and fourth conditions, and the court's satisfaction)`

`the later conditions: all met` MEANS `s 917 the later conditions` OF (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), TRUE
`the later conditions: second not met` MEANS `s 917 the later conditions` OF (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), TRUE
`the later conditions: third not met` MEANS `s 917 the later conditions` OF (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE), TRUE
`the later conditions: fourth not met` MEANS `s 917 the later conditions` OF (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), TRUE
`the later conditions: court not satisfied` MEANS `s 917 the later conditions` OF (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE
`the later conditions: second not known` MEANS `s 917 the later conditions` OF NOTHING, (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), TRUE

`website answer: met` MEANS JUST TRUE
`website answer: not met` MEANS JUST FALSE
`website answer: not asked` MEANS JUST FALSE

§§ `Assertions: the day count and the gates`

-- Fifteen January to fifteen February 2026 is 31 days; the earliest date is that date's day number.
#ASSERT (`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the days from the publication to the earliest date` `publication: 15 January 2026`) EQUALS 31
-- Thirty-one January 2026: 28 February is one day too early (its date one month before is 28 January), so the earliest date is 1 March, 29 days later.
#ASSERT (`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the days from the publication to the earliest date` `publication: 31 January 2026`) EQUALS 29
-- Thirty-one January 2028 (a leap year): 29 February 2028 is too early for the same reason, so the earliest date is 1 March 2028, 30 days later.
#ASSERT (`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the days from the publication to the earliest date` `publication: 31 January 2028`) EQUALS 30
-- First March 2026: the first date one month later is 1 April 2026, 31 days later.
#ASSERT (`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the days from the publication to the earliest date` `publication: 1 March 2026`) EQUALS 31
-- The helper agrees with the existing s 917(3A) test on both sides of the boundary (15 January publication).
#ASSERT (`s 917(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied` `publication: 15 January 2026` (Date 15 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 917(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied` `publication: 15 January 2026` (Date 14 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The helper agrees with the existing s 917(3A) test on both sides of the boundary (31 January publication).
#ASSERT (`s 917(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied` `publication: 31 January 2026` (Date 1 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 917(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied` `publication: 31 January 2026` (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day number of the earliest date is the day number of 15 February 2026.
#ASSERT (`ss 916(3A), 917(3A) and 918(2A) the day number of the earliest date` `publication: 15 January 2026`) EQUALS (Day (Date 15 2 2026))
-- s 917(1): a merger by absorption where all the relevant securities are held; not where they are not all held, and not for a merger by formation of a new company.
#ASSERT `ss 915-918 section 917 applies to the scheme` `scheme: absorption, all securities held`
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 915-918 section 917 applies to the scheme` `scheme: absorption, nothing held`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 915-918 section 917 applies to the scheme` `scheme: formation of a new company`))
-- s 918(1): any merger by absorption, whatever the holding; not a merger by formation of a new company.
#ASSERT `ss 915-918 section 918 applies to the scheme` `scheme: absorption, all securities held`
#ASSERT `ss 915-918 section 918 applies to the scheme` `scheme: absorption, nothing held`
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 915-918 section 918 applies to the scheme` `scheme: formation of a new company`))

§§ `Traces: s 917, the court's order, the one-month wait from the publication on 15 January 2026`

-- s 917(3A): the court makes its order on day 40, well after the first date one month later (day 31); the other conditions are met.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 40

-- s 917(3A): the court's order is dated day 31, 15 February 2026, exactly one month after the publication: "at least one month before the date of the court's order".
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 31

-- s 917(3A): the court's order is dated day 30, 14 February 2026, one day short of a month after the publication.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 30

-- s 917(3A): the court's order is dated on the day of the publication itself.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 0

-- s 917(3A): the court's order is dated day 10, well inside the month.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 10

-- s 917(2): the month has run and the conditions are met, but the court has not made its order; the text gives the court no time, so the power stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 917(1): not all the relevant securities of the transferor company are held by the transferee company, so s 917 does not apply and the rule gives no step.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 917(1): a merger by formation of a new company is not a merger by absorption, so s 917 does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: formation of a new company` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 917(4): the second condition is not met, so the court cannot be satisfied and the route is closed; no step is open after the wait.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: second not met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 917(4C): the third condition (copies free of charge) is not met, so the route is closed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: third not met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 917(5): the fourth condition is not met (members holding 5% required a meeting), so the route is closed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: fourth not met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 917(2): the court is not satisfied that the conditions have been complied with, so the route is closed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: court not satisfied` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 917(4): the answer of the second condition is not known (NOTHING); it is not met, so the court's power is not open (the fork line of the module).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: second not known` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

§§ `Traces: s 917(3B), the website route, the same wait`

-- s 917(3B)(b): the Gazette notice mentioned in s 906A(4) was published on 15 January 2026 and the court's order is dated day 31, a month later; (a) and (c) are met.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` TRUE `website answer: met` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 31

-- s 917(3B)(b): the court's order is dated day 30, one day short of a month after the Gazette notice.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` TRUE `website answer: met` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 30

-- s 917(3B)(a) and (c): the conditions of s 906A(2) to (4), or the availability of the draft terms on the website, are not met, so the first condition fails by that route and the route is closed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 15 January 2026` TRUE `website answer: not met` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

§§ `Traces: s 917(3A), a notice published on the last day of a month`

-- s 917(3A): the notice was published on 31 January 2026; an order dated day 28, 28 February 2026, is not "at least one month" after it (the date one month before 28 February is 28 January).
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 31 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 28

-- s 917(3A): the notice was published on 31 January 2026; an order dated day 29, 1 March 2026, is at least one month after it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 917(2) the court's order that no meeting is required, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held` `publication: 31 January 2026` FALSE `website answer: not asked` `the later conditions: all met` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the court` DOES `s 917(2) the court makes the order that no meeting of the members of any of the merging companies is required` AT 29

§§ `Traces: ss 916(3A) and 918(2A), the first meeting of the transferor company`

-- s 918(2A): the first meeting of the transferor company is held on day 40, after the first date one month later than the publication in respect of the transferee company.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, the transferee relies on section 916(2)` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company` DOES `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme` AT 40

-- s 918(2A): the first meeting is held on day 31, exactly one month after the publication.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, the transferee relies on section 916(2)` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company` DOES `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme` AT 31

-- s 918(2A): the first meeting is held on day 30, one day short of a month after the publication.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a first meeting one day short of the month loses the exemption of the transferee company and is no breach by the transferor company (src:12765, src:12767)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, the transferee relies on section 916(2)` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company` DOES `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme` AT 30

-- s 916(3A): the first meeting is held on the day of the publication itself.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a first meeting on the day of publication loses the exemption of the transferee company and is no breach by the transferor company (src:12765, src:12767)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, the transferee relies on section 916(2)` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company` DOES `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme` AT 0

-- s 918(1): a merger by absorption in which the transferee holds none of the securities and relies on neither s 916(2) nor s 918(1): it holds its own meeting, so the month is no condition of anything and a meeting on day 10 is lawful.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: where the transferee company relies on neither s 916(2) nor s 918(1) it holds its own meeting, and an early first meeting of the transferor company is lawful (src:12765, src:12767)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, nothing held` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company` DOES `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme` AT 10

-- s 918(1), (2A): the transferee company holds none of the securities and relies on s 918(1); the first meeting of the transferor company on day 10 is early, so the exemption is lost and the transferee company's meeting is required (a closed route, no breach).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, nothing held, the transferee relies on section 918(1)` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 915-918 the transferor company` DOES `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the transferor company holds the first meeting of its members summoned to agree to the scheme` AT 10

-- s 918(2A): the month has run and no meeting is held yet; the text gives the transferor company no time to hold it, so the power stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: absorption, all securities held, the transferee relies on section 916(2)` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 918(1): a merger by formation of a new company is not a merger by absorption, so ss 916 and 918 do not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 916(3A) and 918(2A) the first meeting of the transferor company, not before the one-month wait` `scheme: formation of a new company` `publication: 15 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
-- 26 traces; 20 read the same class on the unstable binary (l4-unstable-20261125-a50cbd0) and on the stable line (the stable build 112); all 15 assertions are satisfied on both.
-- The 6 that differ are all the same shape: an event arrives after the prohibition's window has run out, and the MAY that follows it should take the event. Unstable reads FULFILLED; main leaves
-- the MAY open and reads RESIDUAL (the "event after a wait device" difference). The six:
--   1. s 917(3A): the court's order on day 40 (route A, all conditions met)
--   2. s 917(3A): the court's order on day 31, exactly one month after the publication
--   3. s 917(3B)(b): the court's order on day 31, the website route
--   4. s 917(3A): the notice published on 31 January 2026 and the court's order on day 29 (1 March 2026)
--   5. s 918(2A): the first meeting of the transferor company on day 40
--   6. s 918(2A): the first meeting of the transferor company on day 31
-- The BREACH traces (an event inside the window), the traces that wait with no event, and the traces whose gate fails read the same on both.
